# Build context for `az acr build` (the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so whatever
# survives this file is baked into the prod image).
#
# DO NOT widen the bare `*.md` pattern below to a recursive one.
# Docker matches each pattern against the FULL path relative to the context root
# and `*` never crosses a `/`, so bare `*.md` drops only TOP-LEVEL markdown.
# That is load-bearing: the agent fleet reads 12 nested `prompt.md` files at
# IMPORT time (`intelligence/agents/*/definition.py`, plus
# `entities/invoice/intelligence/prompt.md`) via `Path(...).read_text()`.
# A recursive markdown pattern would exclude all of them and the container would
# die on startup with FileNotFoundError before serving a single request.
#
# The same matching rule is why the cache patterns appear twice: the bare form
# for the top level, the `**/` form for nested copies (511 nested `__pycache__`
# dirs, 27 MB, were shipping into the prod image before 2026-11-11).
# Mirrors build.one.mcp/.dockerignore; keep the two in step.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Python
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs and samples
samples/
*.md
!README.md

# Tests
tests/
*_test.py
test_*.py
